  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The comparative",
     "texto": [
      "The usual pattern is to add **-er** to the adjective: billig → **billiger** (cheaper), schön → **schöner** (prettier). Many short adjectives add an umlaut: groß → **größer**, alt → **älter**, jung → **jünger**. **Teuer** loses an «e»: **teurer**.",
      "To say «more» with quantities, **mehr** is used (**mehr Kaffee**, more coffee), not with all adjectives. Some words have special forms: **gut → besser** (good → better), **viel → mehr** (much → more), **gern → lieber** (gladly → prefer).",
      "«Than» is **als**: **Das weiße Handy ist billiger als das schwarze.** For equality: **so … wie** (**as… as**)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Comparatives",
